{"text":"Recent work supports gradually introducing informative negatives rather than immediately selecting the highest-scoring items. [R²NS (WWW 2026)](https://renzhaochun.github.io/assets/pdf/WWW_2026_Camera_Ready.pdf) combines uniform-sampling warm-up, efficient catalog-wide candidate recall, and curriculum reranking; it addresses early training instability and false negatives. [Scalable Cross-Entropy (RecSys 2024)](https://dspace.mit.edu/entities/publication/5392aca9-0bae-4176-9b3a-a8165957ba26) instead approximates full cross-entropy using maximum-inner-product selection of informative outputs. These provide sampling/objective ideas compatible in principle with retaining NextItNet’s causal dilated-convolution backbone; they do not establish gains on this benchmark.

[Correcting the LogQ Correction (RecSys 2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.09331) identifies a subtle sampled-softmax error: the positive is always included, whereas negatives are sampled. Its revised derivation treats those contributions separately and introduces an uncertainty-dependent weight, reporting improvements over standard logQ correction. Sampling correction addresses proposal-distribution bias; it does not identify genuinely relevant unobserved items. Earlier [UFNRec](https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.04116) explicitly handles suspected false negatives through positive reassignment and teacher-provided soft labels, illustrating the distinction.

For Electronics, a reasonable experimental hypothesis is one NextItNet model trained with multiple negatives, uniform warm-up, then moderate-hardness sampling while excluding known training positives. Compare uncorrected sampled cross-entropy against a correction matched to the actual sampling distribution; deterministic top-k mining cannot simply inherit a popularity-based logQ formula. Treat suspected false negatives conservatively rather than automatically relabeling them. Select using the fixed four-category macro validation HR@10: improved training margins or CDs_and_Vinyl separation alone cannot demonstrate better Electronics ranking."}
